ManiT is a balanced ternary programming language targeting
photonic-ternary hardware (The THATTE Device). The compiler
produces both LLVM IR (for binary host execution) and T3ISA
(for native ternary hardware).

Patent applications covering the underlying hardware have been
filed with the Indian Patent Office (Application Nos.
202621045270–202621045342, filed 9 April 2026).

